{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2018c6219dfb72dfd0acb9ebefb027838218775f1c7f0a1ab9d19730b0b678e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b6b229c6c98bd40bf81d216025c310e145ae81d11c5b904b59e8e1ddb6ae64a"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"Prerequisites are bash 4.4+, git 2.20+, and python3 3.8+; PyYAML is optional (needed for fw serve and some helpers), and Node.js is optional with Python as fallback for TypeScript hooks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_250b88293dd96367dea437f48198c698874a270823a7a6962d13fd8789b0a5ff","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5d68eb4b06bfe228f619ee292b76ad014987408b682f5d0ae1a59112ca3f62db"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"Approval verbs such as fw inception decide, fw arc close, and fw bvp confirm refuse to run under agent control and route to a human via the Watchtower dashboard.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_42ed3a22da230600e92df9644d8e4aba2d18ddd7d1c987171fb7a92c244a3810","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_06a7922dbadcade6132d9e092b181384cbf92fb4d6263fa7b484466aebd90d2f","slc_0b822a3bfb515f77d82913cf94dbd7a35e5053a0f0d055fa96d3632bedea5cd9"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"Three memory layers persist across sessions: working memory in .context/working/, project memory in .context/project/, and episodic memory of completed tasks in .context/episodic/.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_69d3be32c32edff26ad8273753fad67457672887423e022e93b204dd645802f2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d6b30f4178c4c6544c9644934a735fa5078a69e1cc26925d13949c34626c7b5f"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"A Framework MCP server exposes 22 capabilities (16 read-only, 6 agent-authority) to external agents; five sovereignty-bound verbs are deliberately never registered, and agent-authority tools shell out through bin/fw so the same gates fire.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9b4a532ad64f09b6efaea344345be7a19e1f23f3ecb4fac7021de4079306b1bd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2001379ba05d5a44ce4b38de7ebdd6202cebb232289b5529c77443b17fd29fe0"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"The framework's core principle is traceability: nothing gets done without a task, with conversations, decisions, and artefacts captured in a record called the Context Fabric.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9eed03bd4cd462e36b284541bccf52cd447c1b05748aa80c398525f2dc3d9d32","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b822a3bfb515f77d82913cf94dbd7a35e5053a0f0d055fa96d3632bedea5cd9","slc_22504f3847f415708dd60d63c5828ae90cd7afad6bf0adc24917e7a5386cefa0","slc_9fd637dc8a97db55cc739305fb5eb427d59b94d5949711297aac7fb1aab4b2ec"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"`fw recall` searches learnings, patterns, decisions, and episodics by meaning rather than keyword, and `fw handover --commit` writes a structured handover the next session reads on start.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a703d06855b41af1fde2da0f877a5009fd53ed865795dc0dde14b0712c1c7e12","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_291dbc160d3e650595659e9e9a89605185f5d8554420da5265d7d14d0d3aca1a","slc_4f5ed7fa0b0dbe463d1f6c201ca15ff63f08c4886de11bac4bad1ba529666e26"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"The README states this is alpha software; multi-provider validation for Cursor, Aider, and Devin is designed but not validated, with Claude Code as the tested provider, and Watchtower auto-start is not yet shipped.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b059a7d7ed3b4f852742f9ebbdf01aa4d84bd33e8a7826e6df65d85c24f2f250","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b8eed433626946bc4efbf0c7ad6d6e326fcbf0c168df17af9c0beeb6ba7debe","slc_662eb0a24fbdb82efc645bcf6617fc586e52d30774947036c5e520fc60ff3062"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"A PreToolUse hook intercepts file modifications and refuses edits when no active task is set; build tasks with placeholder acceptance criteria are blocked (policy G-020).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ba79378d9de5b1295aa6257570eb695a44253e321db25d1227ec501fa61aa929","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0dd225ebb95459860c9914768d9aad35bcd6ba439b55ff911854038778420020"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"The product exposes a `fw` CLI (about 60 verbs across 11 sections) including work-on, audit, recall, fabric blast-radius, handover, serve, tier0 approve, and mcp lifecycle commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_de5e41cb55dc06640216ad9b756eed5fce68c429f99802f8d765a5da1578f526","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_33e4b8c9689de56930c90c33a6233c7cf89380a6efeda5f3296ebb33b10bc1d6"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"A Component Fabric maps how code pieces relate, making a change's blast radius visible before the change rather than after.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e83bc772c0ce2638c050d92f148cd129ffa3c080779829852e69977d23911b75","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_acbe64eaafabf063efc8d1428e57821b0f2f25afae6221ee7e7ae71a3e0c6024"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"A tiered authority model: Tier 0 destructive commands need human approval via `fw tier0 approve`, Tier 1 edits need an active task, Tier 2 exceptions are single-use and logged, Tier 3 read-only is pre-approved.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f1ff934219c8c2b10fde5cb3797cd1c5909e737680e6e3d7a51a33eda92a447f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_43653db9636717250d666bc5a0b677703a4598d8027df6ce7253dce6a4c660bf","slc_c38647422f18195d47c92bb8c208fde1b4c40478449782afebcdbac9b7606f5a"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"The framework wraps an external TermLink binary for cross-terminal, cross-host worker sessions, with bus manifest/read, dispatch send over SSH, and pickup verbs for coordination.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f89df1ec02466e948c27e6ae512cda5579b82e707546d9a13546668e5ab43656","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"dimitrigeelen/agentic-engineering-framework@35aaaaedc1c3 snapshot a8e042de383354ce","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3baf51552bc4eb2fb533ab8e489ed87430ca728e4a62ea68992dea528bb3e053","slc_4b2e20ce9c9ea0d8d49eb30687531261f6e2047b57ffd6077986d8c5ebab7fb5","slc_b55fd58775af6390a140a118cef4ec7585b4d6fdb4a604994f9dea777aa131b8"],"source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"text":"The framework coordinates agents but does not execute them; it is not an agent runtime or multi-agent pipeline, and the model lives in the user's CLI agent while governance lives here.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
